      "paragraphs": [
        "A little more clarity",
        "Business Analytics is decision-focused: statistics, analysis and communication for business questions, comfortable entirely in Excel if that's your team. Data Science goes further into building ML models in Python or R. Teams often run this first.",
        "Yes. Excel carries the full syllabus for most business teams; Python or R come in only if your team wants them. The statistics matter more than the tool.",
        "Before training, we ask for 2–3 real questions your team keeps circling (\"did the price change actually move sales?\"). Those become the working examples, using sanitized data if needed, so the final analysis is genuinely useful, not homework."
      ],
      "content": [
